+++
title = "CLI Reference"
template = "docs"
+++

Every Revela command, grouped the way `revela --help` and the interactive menu show them: **Build**, **Content**, **Setup**, **Addons** and **Info**.

> **Tip:** Add `--help` to any command for its options. Run `revela` without arguments for the interactive menu.

Revela always works on the **current folder** as the project. `cd` into your project folder before running commands.

> **Editions:** Commands marked **Full only** exist in the Full edition and the .NET global tool, but not in Standalone. Standalone has every official plugin and theme built in, so it doesn't need package management. See [Installation](../../get-started/installation/).

---

## Global Options

| Option | Alias | Description |
|--------|-------|-------------|
| `--version` | | Show version information |
| `--help` | `-h`, `-?` | Show help |

---

## Build

### generate

Build your site from source content.

```bash
revela generate all                  # Full pipeline
revela generate scan                 # Scan content and update the manifest
revela generate calendar             # Build calendar data from .ics files (Calendar plugin)
revela generate statistics           # Build EXIF statistics (Statistics plugin)
revela generate pages                # Render HTML pages from the manifest
revela generate images               # Process images from the manifest
revela generate images --force       # Re-encode all images, ignoring what's already done (-f)
revela generate compress             # Pre-compress output with Gzip and Brotli (Compress plugin)
```

`generate all` runs **scan → calendar → statistics → pages → images**. The calendar and statistics steps come from plugins, so the list can be shorter in the Full edition if those plugins aren't installed. Compression is **not** part of `generate all`; run `generate compress` afterwards.

If a step fails, the pipeline stops and suggests `revela check`.

### serve

Preview the generated site on a local HTTP server (Serve plugin).

```bash
revela serve                         # http://localhost:8080
revela serve --port 3000             # Custom port (-p)
revela serve --verbose               # Log every request, not only 404s (-v)
```

### clean

Remove generated files.

```bash
revela clean all                     # output → images → cache → statistics → calendar → compress
revela clean output                  # Delete the output directory and .revela/state (next build re-encodes all images)
revela clean images                  # Delete unused image files (orphaned, old sizes/formats)
revela clean images --dry-run        # Preview only (-d)
revela clean cache                   # Delete .revela/cache (scan manifest, plugin data); keeps .revela/state, so no image is re-encoded
revela clean statistics              # Delete statistics JSON from the cache (Statistics plugin)
revela clean calendar                # Delete calendar JSON from the cache (Calendar plugin)
revela clean compress                # Delete .gz/.br files from the output (Compress plugin)
```

---

## Content

### create page

Create an `_index.revela` file from a template. The path is relative to `source/`.

```bash
revela create page gallery "01 Galleries/Vacation" --title "Summer Vacation"
revela create page text "02 About" --title "About Me"
revela create page statistics "03 Statistics" --title "Photo Statistics"
revela create page calendar "04 Availability" --source bookings.ics --months 12
```

| Option | Alias | Page types | Description |
|--------|-------|------------|-------------|
| `--title` | `-t` | all | Page title |
| `--description` | `-d` | all | Description (for SEO) |
| `--sort` | `-s` | gallery | Sort override, e.g. `dateTaken:asc` |
| `--hidden` | | gallery, text | Hide from navigation |
| `--slug` | | gallery, text | Custom URL segment |
| `--source` | `-s` | calendar | `.ics` file, relative to the page folder (required) |
| `--months` | `-m` | calendar | Number of months to show (default `12`) |

Leave out the path for **interactive mode**:

```bash
revela create page gallery
```

Required options (such as `--source` for a calendar page) must be given: without them, `create page` stops with an error and exit code `1` and writes nothing. Interactive mode asks until you enter a value.

`statistics` and `calendar` come from the Statistics and Calendar plugins. See [Creating Pages](../../guide/pages/).

### source

Download content from external sources.

```bash
revela source onedrive sync                  # Download new and changed files from OneDrive
revela source onedrive sync --dry-run        # Preview only (-n)
revela source onedrive sync --show-files     # List every affected file
revela source onedrive sync --share-url URL  # Use this share link instead of the configured one (-u)
revela source onedrive sync --force          # Re-download all files (-f)
revela source onedrive sync --clean          # Also delete local files that are gone from OneDrive (asks first)
revela source onedrive sync --clean --yes    # Delete without asking (-y); required for --clean outside a terminal
revela source onedrive sync --clean-all      # Delete ALL local files not in OneDrive, ignoring filters

revela source calendar fetch                 # Download all configured iCal feeds into source/
revela source calendar fetch --name bookings # Only one feed (-n)
```

See [OneDrive Source](../../plugins/source-onedrive/) and [Calendar Feeds](../../plugins/source-calendar/).

---

## Setup

### config

Change settings interactively (`revela config`) or directly with options. Most commands open prompts when you run them in a terminal without options. In scripts and CI, always pass options: `config project`, `serve`, `statistics` and `onedrive` without options then show which options to pass and exit with `1`, and `config site` (interactive only) asks you to edit `site.json` directly. The plugin config commands (`onedrive`, `serve`, `statistics`) write `project.json` and need a project.

```bash
revela config                                # Interactive configuration menu

# Project
revela config project --name "My Portfolio" --url https://example.com   # -n, -u
revela config theme --set Lumina             # Select the theme (-s)
revela config theme --viewer lightbox        # Photo viewer: page, lightbox or none
revela config theme --clear-viewer           # Back to the theme's default viewer
revela config paths --source "D:\Photos" --output dist                  # -s, -o
revela config image --formats avif:80,webp:85,jpg:90                    # -f; quality 0 disables a format
revela config site                           # Site metadata in site.json (interactive only)
revela config sorting --galleries asc --field dateTaken --direction desc --fallback filename   # -g, -f, -d

# Source
revela config onedrive --share-url URL       # OneDrive share link (-u)

# Addons
revela config serve --port 3000 --verbose    # -p, -v
revela config statistics --max-entries 20 --sort-by-count false          # -m, -s

# Other
revela config locations                      # Show where configuration files and installed packages live
```

Package feeds (**Full only**):

```bash
revela config feed list                                           # List feeds
revela config feed add releases /absolute/path/to/revela-packages # Add a folder or NuGet v3 URL
revela config feed remove releases                                # Remove a feed (asks when no name is given)
```

See [Configuration](../../guide/configuration/).

### check

Check your project for problems without generating anything. Start here whenever something doesn't work.

```bash
revela check                         # Run every check (same as check all)
revela check all
revela check config                  # Configuration files and values
revela check structure               # Project structure
revela check theme                   # Theme
revela check content                 # Content and front matter
revela check slugs                   # Gallery URLs
revela check calendar                # Calendar .ics files (Calendar plugin)
```

Each problem comes with the file and a suggested fix. The command exits with `2` when it finds an error. Hints and warnings don't change the exit code. Checks only run when you call `revela check`; `generate` doesn't run them first, but a failing step points you to `revela check`.

---

## Addons

### theme

```bash
revela theme list                    # Available themes
revela theme list --online           # Also list themes from NuGet feeds (-o)
revela theme files                   # Files of the active theme and where they come from
revela theme files --theme Lumina    # A specific theme (-t)
revela theme extract Lumina          # Copy the whole theme to themes/Lumina/
revela theme extract Lumina MyTheme  # Copy it under another name
revela theme extract Lumina --file Assets/main.css   # Only a file or folder (-F)
revela theme extract Lumina --force  # Overwrite without asking (-f)
```

Install and remove themes (**Full only**):

```bash
revela theme install Lumina.Statistics       # By short name or full package ID
revela theme install --all                   # All available themes (-a)
revela theme uninstall Lumina.Statistics     # Asks for confirmation; --yes (-y) skips it
```

`theme install` accepts `--version` (`-v`), `--source` (`-s`, feed name or URL) and `--allow-project-feeds`, like `plugin install`. Installing a theme by name reads the package type from the package itself, so no `packages refresh` is needed; only `--all` and the interactive picker (no name) list themes from the package index. A plugin package passed to `theme install` (or a theme package passed to `plugin install`) is rejected with a hint to the right command.

### plugin (Full only)

```bash
revela plugin list                           # Installed plugins
revela plugin install Statistics             # By short name
revela plugin install Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Statistics   # By package ID
revela plugin install Statistics --version 1.2.0           # Specific version (-v)
revela plugin install MyPlugin --source https://my-feed.example.com/v3/index.json   # Feed name or URL (-s)
revela plugin install --all                  # All available plugins (-a)
revela plugin install Statistics --allow-project-feeds     # Use project.json feeds without asking
revela plugin uninstall Statistics           # Asks for confirmation; --yes (-y) skips it
```

Install commands record the exact installed version under `dependencies.packages` in exactly one file: `project.json` when you run them inside a project, otherwise the global `revela.json`. Uninstall removes the entry from that same file.

### packages (Full only)

```bash
revela packages refresh              # Update the local package index from all feeds
revela packages search               # List all packages in the index
revela packages search calendar      # Search by name
revela packages search --type theme  # Only themes or only plugins (-t theme|plugin)
```

### restore (Full only)

Install the themes and plugins a project needs.

```bash
revela restore                       # Install missing dependencies
revela restore --check               # Only report what's missing
revela restore --allow-project-feeds # Use feeds declared in project.json without asking
```

Useful after cloning a project or updating Revela. Installs every package in `dependencies.packages` (from `revela.json` and `project.json`) that isn't installed yet, plus the package that provides `theme.name`. Restored versions are pinned only for entries that `project.json` itself declares; packages declared only in your global `revela.json` are installed but not copied into the project. Feeds declared only in `project.json` need your confirmation; non-interactive runs stop unless you pass `--allow-project-feeds`. See [Dependencies and Feeds](../../guide/configuration/#dependencies-and-feeds).

---

## Info

```bash
revela info                          # Version, edition, runtime and active theme
```

In the **Standalone** edition `revela info` also lists every built-in plugin and theme with its version. In the **Full** edition use `revela plugin list` and `revela theme list` for the installed packages. `revela --version` prints just the version line, ending with the edition (`— Standalone edition` or `— Full edition`).

In the interactive menu, installing and uninstalling plugins and themes is not offered: the running menu has the package files loaded and cannot replace them safely. Run those commands from the command line (or use the setup wizard for packages that are not installed yet), then start Revela again.

---

## Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `0` | Success |
| `1` | Error or cancelled; see the output |
| `2` | Configuration problem (invalid JSON or setting), or `revela check` found an error |

Handy for scripting: treat any non-zero code as a failure. Running `revela` without arguments outside a terminal (for example in CI) exits with `1`; always pass a command there.

---

## Automation & CI

Use the **Standalone** edition in CI: it's one download with everything built in, and no .NET SDK is needed. This is how [revela.website](https://revela.website) itself is built:

```yaml
name: Build site
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Download Revela (Standalone, newest release)
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        run: |
          TAG=$(gh release list --repo Spectara/Revela --limit 1 --json tagName --jq '.[0].tagName')
          gh release download "$TAG" --repo Spectara/Revela --pattern "revela-linux-x64-standalone.tar.gz"
          tar -xzf revela-linux-x64-standalone.tar.gz
          chmod +x ./revela

      - name: Generate site
        run: ./revela generate all

      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: website
          path: output/
```

To pin a version for reproducible builds, replace `$TAG` with a tag such as `v0.0.1-beta.21`. The [Deployment guide](../../guide/deployment/) shows how to publish the result to GitHub Pages and other hosts.

---

## Tab Completion (optional)

Revela is built on System.CommandLine, so your shell can tab-complete commands, subcommands, options, and enum values. It's a one-time setup per machine and shell (bash, zsh, PowerShell, but not `cmd.exe`):

1. Install the `dotnet-suggest` global tool:

   ```bash
   dotnet tool install -g dotnet-suggest
   ```

2. Add the `dotnet-suggest` shim to your shell profile. See [Microsoft's tab-completion guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/standard/commandline/tab-completion) for the exact snippet for bash, zsh, or PowerShell.

3. Register the Revela executable:

   ```bash
   dotnet-suggest register --command-path /path/to/revela
   ```

Restart your shell. Now `revela gen<Tab>` expands to `generate`, and `revela generate <Tab>` lists `all`, `scan`, `pages`, `images`, and the plugin steps.
